{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790259189,"nonce":"QZP1iuLDM63hj3J8hZADOpfp/+E=","message":"The same limit reaches += on a list behind a dynamic value (zb_any_arith_inplace, commit 4b53841a): a boxed list of one kind (int, float or str) grows in place only when every new value is of that kind; otherwise it falls back to zb_any_arith and the name is rebound to a new list of dynamic values, so an alias bound before the statement keeps the old list. `ys = [1, 2]; same = ys; ys += (3,); ys += ('a',)` leaves `same` at [1, 2, 3] where CPython has [1, 2, 3, 'a']. Widening the kinded literal as this issue proposes removes that case too.","files":null}]}